39534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423902 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423900 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423902 1069 "q-96575" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423902 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423902 1071 "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X=-6)$ can be approximated as" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423902 1072 #uuid "39bb09ec-48b5-5f33-adde-628ba380f524" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423902 1074 "We construct an interval around $X=-6$ with a radius of $0.5:$\n\n![](images/9f/9f21d7fe3ba1f4efa7b4e24e3d096d84825ff3712f5854c76dabccf0477f503c.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=-6) & ≈P(-6-0.5\\le Y\\le -6+0.5) \\\\  & =P(-6.5\\le Y\\le -5.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423903 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423897 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423903 1069 "q-96643" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423903 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423903 1071 "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(2<X<7)$ can be approximated as" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423903 1072 #uuid "a5c8fffc-11c1-576d-8ffb-d7561ffc582e" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423903 1074 "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequalities as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<7) & =P(3\\le X\\le 6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoints of the interval $3\\le X\\le 6$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 6) & ≈P(3-0.5\\le Y\\le 6+0.5) \\\\  & =P(2.5\\le Y\\le 6.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423904 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423899 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423904 1069 "q-132226" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423904 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423904 1071 "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(4\\le X\\le 11)$ can be approximated as" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423904 1072 #uuid "acbfdb28-97bf-5853-92f1-7b02234a722c" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423904 1074 "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we extend the endpoints of the interval $4\\le X\\le 11$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4\\le X\\le 11) & ≈P(4-0.5\\le Y\\le 11+0.5) \\\\  & =P(3.5\\le Y\\le 11.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423905 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423898 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423905 1069 "q-132239" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423905 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423905 1071 "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X>19)$ can be approximated as" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423905 1072 #uuid "c629c32e-40e8-52bc-a310-6147fcdaffe0" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true] [17592186423905 1074 "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequality as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X>19)=P(X\\ge 20)\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoints of the interval $X\\ge 20$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 20) & ≈P(Y\\ge 20-0.5) \\\\  & =P(Y\\ge 19.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534513 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-055ee122-3724-57f6-b149-fab95924d791" 17592186423866 "answer-162d5e12-0ad8-5ea1-80fb-a59cd473cd6d" 17592186423867 "answer-1f6c0067-ea4d-59fa-8a3a-c55e51a9774c" 17592186423868 "answer-26f1787c-1530-51d1-a55f-5b4548e5e9af" 17592186423869 "answer-2d1